senses.gloss:
सम्-√ भू P. Ā. -भवति, ˚ते (ind.p. -भूय, q.v.), to be or come together, assemble, meet, be joined or united with (instr. with or without सह, or loc.), RV. &c. &c.;
to be united sexually with (instr. with or without सह, or सार्धम्, or acc.), AV.; ŚBr.; MBh. &c.;
to be born or produced from (abl.), arise, spring up, develop, ib.;
to happen, occur, be, be found, exist, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to be possible, Hit.; Vedāntas.;
to be or become anything (nom.), RV.; Br.; MBh.;
to accrue to, fall to the share of (loc. or gen.), R.; Kathās.;
to prevail, be effective, ŚBr.;
to be able to or capable of (inf. or loc.), Śiś.;
to enter into, partake of, attain to (acc.), Yājñ.;
to find room in, be contained in or numbered among (loc.), RV.; MBh. &c.;
to be adequate, MBh.;
to be capable of holding, Pāṇ. v, 1, 52 :
Caus. -भावयति, to cause to be together, bring together, present or affect any one (acc.) with (instr.; with दोषेण, ‘to attach blame to’, with अन्नेन, ‘to give food to’), Kāv.; Kathās.; BhP. ;
to cause to be born or produced, effect, accomplish, make, AitBr.; MBh. &c.;
to foster, cherish, MBh.;
to resort to (acc.), ib.;
to meet with, find (जीवन्तीम्, ‘alive’), Hcar.;
to honour, revere, salute, greet, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to receive or accept graciously, Pañcat.;
to imply, suggest a possibility, suppose anything possible in any one (loc. or gen.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to regard or consider as (two acc.), Kālid.; Pañcat.;
to think it possible that (Pot. with and without यद्, or fut.), Pāṇ. iii, 3, 155, Sch.;
 (with न) to think it impossible that (Pot. with and without यद्, यच्च, यत्र, यदा, यदि, or जातु; fut. with and without किं किल), Pāṇ. iii, 3, 145 &c. Sch.;
 (Ā.) to reach, arrive at (acc.), Pat. :
Pass. of Caus. -भाव्यते, to be brought about or together &c. (see above);
to be (thought) possible or probable or fitting or consistent, Mṛcch.; Kālid. &c.:
Desid. -बुभूषति, to wish to thrive or prosper, ŚāṅkhŚr.

सम्-√ भा P. -भाति, to shine fully or brightly, be very bright, TBr.;
to shine forth, be visible or conspicuous, MBh.;
to appear, seem to be (nom. with and without इव, or यथा), ib.; R. &c.

सम्-√ भज् P. Ā. -भजति, ˚ते, to distribute completely, share, bestow, grant, Sāy.;
 (Ā.) to cause to participate in, present with a gift, PārGṛ.; MBh.;
to divide, Sūryas.

सम्-√ भाष् Ā. -भाषते (pr. p. in MBh. also -भाषत्), to speak together, converse with (instr. with or without सह), Gaut.; Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to speak to (acc.), address, greet, salute, KauṣUp.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to join in a conversation, Vait.;
to agree, consent, enter into an engagement, R.;
to talk over, persuade, Hit.;
to speak, say, recite, Hariv.;
to have sexual intercourse with, MW. :
Caus. -भाषयति (ind.p. -भाषित्वा v.l. in B. for -भाषयित्वा), to converse with (instr.), Hariv.;
to speak to, address (acc.), R.;
to persuade, prevail upon (v.l. for -भावयति), MBh.

सम्-√ भिद् P. Ā. -भिनत्ति, -भिन्त्ते, to break to pieces, split or break completely asunder, pierce, hurt, AV. &c. &c.;
to bring into contact, combine, join, mingle, TS. &c. &c.;
to associate with (acc.), SaddhP.

सम्-√ 3. भुज् P. Ā. -भुनक्ति, -भुङ्क्ते, (aor. Subj. -भुजम्, RV.) to eat together, make a meal in common, AV.; Āpast.;
to enjoy (esp. carnally), Rājat.;
to partake of (gen.), RV. ii, 1, 4 :
Caus. -भोजयति, to cause to enjoy or eat, feed any one (acc.) with (instr.), Yājñ.; MBh.; BhP.

सम्-√ भृ P. Ā. -भरति, ˚ते (Ved. pf. -जभार), to draw together, roll or fold up, RV. i, 115, 4;
 (Ā.) to close (the jaws), ib. x, 79, 1;
to bring together, gather, collect, unite, compose, arrange, prepare, make ready, procure (materials or ingredients of any kind, esp. for a sacrifice; with सम्-भारान्˚, ‘to collect all requisites’, ‘prepare what is necessary’), RV. &c. &c.;
to pay back, MaitrS.;
to maintain, cherish, R.;
to offer, present, MW. :
Caus. -भारयति, to cause to bring together or prepare, R.

सम्-√ भ्रम् P. भ्रमति, or -भ्राम्यति, to roam or wander all about, go quite astray, Kathās.;
to be greatly confused, be perplexed or puzzled, MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. -भ्रामयति, to lead astray, perplex, bewilder &c.: (only in) Pass. -भ्राम्यते, to be perplexed about, despair of (abl.), MBh.
